pages.content:
A binary search tree is a special type of tree where for every node, the left child of that node is smaller than the node and the right child is greater. Check out the tree below for better understanding:      


img {
  display: block;
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-right: auto;
}






Few properties of BST (Binary Search Tree) are:       

 - The value of every node in the left subtree for a node `x` is smaller than the value of `x`, and this is true for all nodes in the tree.     
 - Similarly, the value of all nodes in the right subtree is larger.
 - The left and right subtree for any node are also binary search trees.    

The properties mentioned above help us to apply binary search for operations.           
Time Complexity for Search, Insert, Delete operations:       

Binary Tree - O(n)       
Binary Search Tree - O(h)   
where `h` is the height of tree which is log2(n) in best case when the tree is balanced.

